CHAPTER.VERS:
And Jesus began to say to them, Take heed that no man leads you

          {+}
         astray.

And when you

          {+}
         will hear of wars and rumors of wars, don't be troubled: [these things] must surely come to pass; but the end is not yet.

But you

          {+}
         take heed to yourselves. They will deliver you

          {+}
         up to Sanhedrins; and in synagogues you

          {+}
         will be beaten; and before governors and kings you

          {+}
         will stand for my sake, for a testimony to them.

And when they lead you

          {+}
         [to judgment], and deliver you

          {+}
         up, don't be anxious beforehand what you

          {+}
         will speak: but whatever will be given you

          {+}
         in that hour, that speak

          {+}
        ; for it is not you

          {+}
         who speak, but the Holy Spirit.

And you

          {+}
         will be hated of all men for my name's sake: but he who endures to the end, the same will be saved.

But when you

          {+}
         see the detestable thing of desolation standing where it ought not (let him who reads understand), then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains:

And pray

          {+}
         that it is not in the winter.

And then if any man will say to you

          {+}
        , Look, here is the Christ; or, Look, there; don't believe [it]:

But take

          {+}
         heed: I have told you

          {+}
         all things beforehand.

Now from the fig tree learn her parable: when her branch has now become tender, and puts forth its leaves, you

          {+}
         know that the summer is near;

even so you

          {+}
         also, when you

          {+}
         see these things coming to pass, know

          {+}
         that it is near, [even] at the doors.

Truly I say to you

          {+}
        , This generation will not pass away, until all these things be accomplished.

Take

          {+}
         heed, watch

          {+}
        : for you

          {+}
         don't know when the time is.

Watch therefore: for you

          {+}
         don't know when the lord of the house comes, whether at evening, or at midnight, or at rooster crowing, or in the morning;

lest coming suddenly he find you

          {+}
         sleeping.

And what I say to you

          {+}
         I say to all, Watch.
